{
  "description": "What POST /api/agent/claim answers and how `vibememory connect` reads it: curl's exit code, the HTTP status (200 when omitted) and the body in, the claim or the reason out. `body` is the JSON the cabinet sends, `raw` the literal stdout. The cabinet's int test checks its answers carry exactly the fields of `token` and `key`. Tokens are synthetic: the secret is one repeated character, as the privacy gate requires. `asked` is the cabinet the code was sent to, as `connect --cabinet` took it; a case may ask another.",
  "asked": "https://app.vibememory.ru",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "token",
      "provenance": "computed",
      "note": "The answer the cabinet gives for a token claim; the cabinet's test checks its own answer has exactly these fields.",
      "exit": 0,
      "body": {
        "version": 1,
        "kind": "token",
        "cabinet": "https://app.vibememory.ru",
        "team": "vibebrains",
        "member": "alice",
        "agent": "claude-code",
        "tokenId": "tk_7q2m9x4a",
        "token": "vmt_7q2m9x4a_1111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111",
        "mcpUrl": "https://vibememory.ru/mcp"
      },
      "expect": {
        "token": {
          "team": "vibebrains",
          "member": "alice",
          "agent": "claude-code",
          "tokenId": "tk_7q2m9x4a"
        }
      }
    },
